                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Honestly I thought the game had a lot of great aspects until I got to the \"end\" after an hour of gameplay. It's barely a chapter length so trying to charge $5 is ridiculous. THIS SHOULD BE A FREE DEMO, considering it ends with a \"to be continued\" message. The developers promise a part 2 and I haven't seen news about it whatsoever, being that the game is from 2018 there should be some update or information. It feels kind of scammy for the developer/publisher \"LoopyMood\" to have this as their only title with nothing to show for the past 8 years yet still be bold enough to charge money. There's potential in the game as I enjoyed the overall story, visuals, gameplay and puzzles; there was just the right amount of challenge without being too challenging, with the hints it can be easier but there is a cooldown timer so you don't repeatedly use it. If the developers actually commit to finishing this project I could see it being successful and potentially (with all of the chapters) being worth the price tag but not in it's current state. Not to mention I've played several games of similar or better quality than this that were offered for free. (Poco, Samorost 1, ENA: Dream BBQ, Emily is Away, Homesick, Serena, Draw, My Beautiful Misinterpretation of Words, Yume Nikki, The Mirror Lied)",
